All rings, except chargeable rings at +0, make you a little hungry.
(Rings of regeneration and hunger, and possibly conflict as well, make
you more than a little hungry)

The ring of slow digestion prevents normal hunger, i.e. what you get
from just being alive, but not hunger from rings, including itself.

The game checks at certain turns whether you have a ring on your left
hand that makes you hungry, and on certain other turns whether you have
a ring on your right hand that makes you hungry.

If you have a ring of slow digestion on each hand, and take the ring off
the hand that's about to be checked, and put it back on as soon as it
has been checked, you will never wear a ring on the hand that's being
checked, so you'll never get hungry from rings; and because you're
still wearing a ring of slow digestion at all times, you'll never get
hungry from just being alive either.

Most people think this is just plain too much hassle.

